         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### The First to Use Their Hands\n\nIn the previous lesson, we saw that we can use our hands to count.\n\nWe cannot say that other animals used their hands to count in the past. But we can find out when hands were used. We can also find out why we are the first species to use them for counting.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "7aa8a22b-cc43-443e-bd1a-45ac98346264",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "7aa8a22b-cc43-443e-bd1a-45ac98346264",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "thinking",
         "source_menu": [],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "Let's start with a reflection: if you started digging a hole in the ground, would you only find earth as the hole got deeper?",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "93c341e9-1aa0-4433-8747-029f96f11d9a",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": "no",
         "score": 2,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "93c341e9-1aa0-4433-8747-029f96f11d9a",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "happy",
         "source_menu": [
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "0be2ea18-ab78-4cb1-b3be-1ff0ba4ade95",
               "text": "Museo Nacional de Antropologia - México",
               "page": "https://www.mna.inah.gob.mx/",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            },
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "ab1dda1e-95c2-4087-8299-e851e58bdc6f",
               "text": "Original Text",
               "page": "index.html?page=tree&arg=33c83383-b9b5-43ec-987d-68f027f342b2",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Expanding Knowledge\n\nSometimes we do not see something. That does not mean it does not exist or never existed. Maybe we just do not know about it.\n\nScientists make holes in the ground, or dig. With this, we can discover what happened in Earth's past. For example, when we find bones like ours and tools next to them, we can say that people in the past used that tool.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<img src=\"https://www.historytracers.org/images/MexicoCityMuseo/HomoSapiens.jpg\" />",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": [],
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "*Image taken during a visit to the Museo Nacional de Antropología - México",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": [],
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "5c8e1349-2f29-4b3e-80d4-76eb8d7e9786",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "5c8e1349-2f29-4b3e-80d4-76eb8d7e9786",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "",
         "source_menu": [
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "a27bf40a-6cf8-4c9a-8b53-efcd80864c83",
               "text": "Fran Dorey. Homo habilis",
               "page": "https://australian.museum/learn/science/human-evolution/homo-habilis/",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2020",
                  "month": "10",
                  "day": "02"
               }
            },
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "e4e24b02-9e06-479a-8f5e-33c6576e79eb",
               "text": "Don Hitchcock",
               "page": "https://donsmaps.com/habilis.html",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2015",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            },
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "ab1dda1e-95c2-4087-8299-e851e58bdc6f",
               "text": "Original Text",
               "page": "index.html?page=tree&arg=33c83383-b9b5-43ec-987d-68f027f342b2",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Skillful Humans\n\nAs scientists keep digging, a moment comes when we stop finding humans like us. But we find humans who lived in the past. They also made tools. Some of them are known as *Homo habilis*.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<img src=\"https://www.historytracers.org/images/DonsMaps/img_6652habilissm.jpg\" />",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": [],
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "*Image made by Don Hitchcock and available on Don's maps.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": [],
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "f6d79260-e367-4313-94c7-3b1aaa2bf6f1",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "f6d79260-e367-4313-94c7-3b1aaa2bf6f1",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "thinking",
         "source_menu": [],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### How Is That Possible?\n\nWhat if the tools found with *Homo habilis* were made by humans like us?\n\nTools change over time. Also, the tools found with them are not like ours.\n\nSo, because of the condition of the tools, the depth where they were found, and their shape, we cannot say they were made by humans like us.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "4af50451-d77e-4285-83c7-7a228fe1a50e",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "4af50451-d77e-4285-83c7-7a228fe1a50e",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "",
         "source_menu": [
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "a4f22e25-5839-407f-a1aa-634521d52b42",
               "text": "Francisco A. González Redondo  et al.",
               "page": "https://doi.org/10.4321/S0211-95362010000100007",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2010",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            },
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "cc8c1467-a6af-4f9c-ba60-ab6df35aba05",
               "text": "Original Text",
               "page": "index.html?page=class_content&arg=7fe341a9-420e-4318-be3e-c7c201d821a8",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2024",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### What About Hands for Counting?\n\nWe saw that other animals made tools. But we never saw them use their hands to count. That is because nothing shows that another animal, besides us, used its hands to count.\n\nBut long before writing was created on any continent, our species already made marks. For example, the marks of our hands on a baboon bone, like the one on this screen.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<img src=\"https://www.historytracers.org/images/ResearchGate/Figura-9-Hueso-de-Lebombo.png\" />",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": [],
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "*Image made by Enrique Silván Pobes.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": [],
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "922797ba-64d5-4ebe-b5e1-a85ff21a4df0",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
        "id": "922797ba-64d5-4ebe-b5e1-a85ff21a4df0",
        "audio": "",
        "smile": "",
        "source_menu": [],
        "text": [
          {
            "text": "#### Conclusion\n\nIn this lesson, we learned how scientists found out that other humans also made tools.\n\nWe also saw that, until another finding appears, we are the first humans to use their hands to count. This happened before we wrote.\n\nIn the next lesson, we will do something similar, but this time with the voice.",
            "source": [],
            "date_time": null,
            "isTable": false,
            "imgdesc": "",
            "format": "markdown",
            "PostMention": ""
          }
        ],
